39, "baseline_margin": -6.55, "analyst_adjustment": -1.45, "key_factors": ["Consistent polling shows Ayotte ahead by high single to low double digits", "Raters uniformly place the race at Lean R or better for Republicans", "Ayotte's incumbency and crossover appeal in a slightly Democratic-leaning state", "Prediction markets price Warmington's chances near 8%"], "rationale": "Every recent poll shows Ayotte leading, with October surveys clustering around an eight-to-ten-point margin, and all eight expert ratings put the race at Lean R or stronger for her. The fundamentals are mixed given New Hampshire's modest Democratic lean, but incumbency and stable polling justify a Likely R rating.", "watch": "A late debate-driven shift or polling error toward Warmington could tighten the race, though no current evidence points that way.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Incumbent Kelly Ayotte (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Incumbent Republican Kelly Ayotte seeks a second term against Democrat Cinde Warmington, with minor candidate Jon Kiper also on the ballot. New Hampshire leans slightly Democratic on paper, but Ayotte has built a durable lead through her first years in office. October polls from Saint Anselm, UMass Lowell, and Rasmussen all show her ahead by eight to ten points, consistent with averages near nine points. Expert raters across the spectrum call the race Likely R or better, and prediction markets give Warmington roughly an eight percent chance. The campaigns have clashed in debates over housing, energy, data centers, taxes, and education, but polling has barely moved all fall. Warmington would need a substantial late shift or a large polling miss to close the gap in the race's final days.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0651, "margin": -8.09}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0566, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0654, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0669, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem":